---
/**
 * The arcade toast stack: transient notices a cabinet raises through
 * `createToaster` in src/games/engine/toast.ts, which is the required shared
 * channel for toast *behaviour*. This component is the matching channel for
 * their markup and presentation, so restyling the floor's toasts is one edit
 * rather than one per cabinet.
 *
 * Drop it inside the positioned wrapper that holds the game canvas and its
 * overlays; the game then mounts it with
 * `createToaster(document.getElementById('toast-area'))`. The `.toast`
 * children are created at runtime by that module, never here, which is why
 * their rule is declared with `:global`.
 *
 * The stack has to paint above the cabinets' `.game-overlay` panels: a run's
 * one-time new-record toast fires in the same breath that raises the
 * game-over or round overlay, and behind a dimmed, blurred panel it is spent
 * without ever being seen. Three cabinets give that overlay `z-index: 2` and
 * the stack precedes the overlays in DOM order, so this must be strictly
 * greater than 2 — an equal value loses the tie to the later sibling. Tank
 * Duel's local `z-index: 2` (PR #251) worked only because its own overlay set
 * no z-index at all.
 */
---

<div id="toast-area" class="toast-area"></div>

<style>
  .toast-area {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: var(--space-md);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    z-index: 3;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .toast-area :global(.toast) {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: 999px;
    animation: toastIn 0.2s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  @keyframes toastIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
</style>
